  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SOS Minas Gerais</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 23 February 2026, extreme rainfall in the Zona da Mata region of Minas Gerais has caused widespread floods and landslides across Juiz de Fora, Ub&#xe1;, and Matias Barbosa, leading to the declaration of a state of public calamity. This emergency is part of a broader national pattern: Brazil has experienced a documented 460% increase in disasters since the 1990s, with extreme events rising annually. This project strengthens both the humanitarian response and emergency preparedness in Minas Gerais by combining coordinated, protection sensitive assistance for flood affected populations with targeted support to local authorities to enhance disaster readiness. The project delivers two complementary outcomes by ensuring that affected populations receive safe, dignified and well coordinated assistance in temporary collective centres, while simultaneously strengthening municipal and community preparedness through improved risk information, enhanced emergency readiness capacities, updated operational protocols and participatory simulations to reduce future disaster impacts and reinforce preparedness and resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
